{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Archimedean","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.binding_not_mass_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.binding_not_mass_sector","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L265-L272","doc":"**The binding multiplier is not a mass multiplier — forced by bar-parity.** The nonzero\nbar-odd count (binding) channel cannot be bar-even, so it can never coincide with a bar-even\nmass/self-trace multiplier. The linking-vs-self-energy assignment is a parity fact, not a modelling\nchoice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.barEven_barOdd_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.barEven_barOdd_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L256-L263","doc":"**The bar sectors are orthogonal:** a function that is both bar-even and bar-odd vanishes on\n`q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.quantumDim2_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.quantumDim2_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L247-L254","doc":"The quantum dimension of the fundamental, `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`, is bar-even (`dim_q = dim_{q⁻¹}`).\n`lw` is a positive average of such quantum dimensions, hence bar-even — the mass multiplier sits in\nthe sector complementary to the binding count channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.countChannel_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.countChannel_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L239-L245","doc":"The unsigned (Coulomb / sinh) count channel is **bar-odd** — its `q − q⁻¹` factor flips sign\nunder `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedChannel_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedChannel_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L231-L237","doc":"The signed (strong / cosh) channel is **bar-even** — its `q + q⁻¹` factor is `q ↦ q⁻¹`\ninvariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.BarOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.BarOdd","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L228-L229","doc":"`f` is **bar-odd**: it changes sign under the bar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` (on `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.BarEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.BarEven","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L225-L226","doc":"`f` is **bar-even**: invariant under the bar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` (on `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.cluster_coordination_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.cluster_coordination_count","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L198-L204","doc":"**Coordination count of a fully-bonded cluster.** If every one of the `C(A,2)` pairs is a\nminimal Brunnian bond (one unit each), the total coordination count is `C(A,2) = A(A−1)/2`,\ni.e. per-nucleon `z = A−1`. This is the `n₊+n₋ → z` map for the canonical carriers; the graph\nstructure (which pairs bond) is `QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.minimal_brunnian_bond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.minimal_brunnian_bond","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L191-L196","doc":"**A minimal Brunnian bond carries exactly one coordination unit.** The pair `n₊ = n₋ = 1`\n(the pairwise crossing pattern inside `L6a4`, linking number 0) has count channel `q − q⁻¹`, i.e.\ncount multiplicity `½(n₊+n₋) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.hopf_multiplicities","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.hopf_multiplicities","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L173-L180","doc":"**The deuteron (Hopf) boundary case.** The positive Hopf carrier has `n₊ = 2`, `n₋ = 0`, so both\nmultiplicities equal `2`: the linking number (`|lk| = 1`) and the coordination count (`z = 1`) give\nthe same multiplier. By `multiplicities_agree_iff` this is exactly because the carrier is\nall-positive — and it is why the two invariants agree for a Hopf-bonded pair and diverge only at\n`A ≥ 3`, where the Brunnian carriers collapse the signed one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedMultiplicity_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedMultiplicity_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L160-L171","doc":"**Maximal separation happens exactly on Brunnian pairs.** The signed (linking-number)\nmultiplicity vanishes iff `n₊ = n₋`. Together with `multiplicities_agree_iff` this brackets the whole\nrange: the two invariants coincide exactly on all-positive carriers, and the signed one dies exactly\non Brunnian ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_multiplicities","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_multiplicities","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L152-L158","doc":"**Brunnian pairs separate the two multiplicities maximally.** The signed multiplicity collapses\nto `0` while the unsigned one is the full crossing count `2m` — the quantitative form of \"only the\ncoordination count survives\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.multiplicities_agree_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.multiplicities_agree_iff","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L141-L150","doc":"**The two multiplicities agree exactly on all-positive braids.** The linking number and the\ncoordination count coincide iff there are no negative inter-component crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.countMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.countMultiplicity","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L138-L139","doc":"The unsigned (crossing / coordination) multiplicity `n₊ + n₋`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedMultiplicity","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L135-L136","doc":"The signed (writhe / linking-number) multiplicity `n₊ − n₋ = 2·lk`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_channels_strict_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_channels_strict_mono","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L108-L124","doc":"**The two mutual invariants genuinely diverge for a Brunnian pair.** The signed channel is\nzero for every `m` (any number of sign-cancelling crossings), while the count channel strictly\nincreases with `m`. So \"linking number\" and \"coordination count\" are not two names for one\nmultiplier: on a Brunnian link they take different values, and only the unsigned one is the\nbinding carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_binding_survives","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_binding_survives","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L94-L106","doc":"**Binding survives the Brunnian vanishing.** For a crossing pair (`m > 0`) at a substrate\nmodulus `q > 1`, the count channel is strictly positive — so the mutual energy is nonzero even\nthough the pairwise linking number is zero. This is the crux of `qou-brng`'s \"surviving route\":\nthe coordination count is the correct, non-vanishing binding multiplier for a Brunnian nuclear\nlink, where the Gauss linking number is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_countChannel_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_countChannel_eq","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L87-L92","doc":"The Brunnian count channel evaluates to `m·(q − q⁻¹)` — proportional to the crossing count\n`m = ½(n₊+n₋)`, not to the (zero) linking number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_energy_is_count_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_energy_is_count_channel","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L80-L85","doc":"**For a Brunnian pair the binding energy IS the unsigned count channel.** With the signed\nchannel empty, the entire mutual/binding energy is carried by the sign-blind coordination-count\nchannel. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:brunnian-binding-channel","label":"prop:brunnian-binding-channel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/brunnian-binding-channel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_signedChannel_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.brunnian_signedChannel_zero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L72-L78","doc":"**A Brunnian pair empties the signed channel.** The Brunnian condition is that the pairwise\nGauss linking number vanishes, i.e. the signed crossing sum is zero (`n₊ = n₋`). Then the\nwrithe-weighted strong channel is identically zero — no signed/linking contribution to binding\nsurvives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.pairEnergy_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.pairEnergy_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L65-L70","doc":"The mutual crossing energy splits into the signed (writhe) and unsigned (count) channels.\nMirrors `QOU.Braiding.CrossingEnergy.decomposition` for the inter-component pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.countChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.countChannel","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L60-L63","doc":"**Unsigned** (Coulomb / sinh) channel: `½(n₊ + n₋)(q − q⁻¹)`. Its multiplicity is the\ncrossing **count** `n₊ + n₋` — sign-blind, i.e. a coordination count rather than a linking\nnumber. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.signedChannel","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L56-L58","doc":"**Signed** (strong / cosh) channel: `½(n₊ − n₋)(q + q⁻¹)`. Its multiplicity is the\n**writhe** `n₊ − n₋ = 2·lk`, the (signed) Gauss linking number — sign-changing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.pairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.pairEnergy","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianBindingChannel.lean#L52-L54","doc":"Skein-signed mutual crossing energy of a component pair with `np` positive and `nn` negative\ninter-component crossings: `n₊·q − n₋·q⁻¹` (the `𝔈_cross(𝓛)` of `def:crossing-energy`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}